  "text": "Làm đềtrực tuyến tại: https://ielts-fighter.com/online-test.html\nWebsite tựhọc IELTS: https://ielts-fighter.com\nHowever, paragraphing is not used effectively to sequence ideas, so more\neffective paragraphing could increase the score.\nThere are some strong examples of vocabulary [comes down to one point |\nforces us to look after the needs of] with some higher-level collocation.\nHowever, the level of error is quite high and detracts from the score for lexis.\nGrammatical range is also fairly wide, but again, the errors and missing\npunctuation mean that the response cannot score more highly.\nTo achieve a higher score, the candidate should provide greater clarity when\nextending the main ideas, and use more effective paragraphing to organise\nideas and improve progression.\n[Reference translation]\nThe overall organization of ideas in the article is generally logical, but there is a\nlack of clear progression in the sections referring to the ownership of water on\nEarth, with repetition across paragraphs 2, 3, and 4.\nHowever, generally, the ideas are arranged in order, and we can still follow\nthe author’s train of thought.\nCohesive devices are used effectively in some places, such as good use of\npronouns within sentences [while | us | who | their own countrymen].\nHowever, the use of paragraphs is not effective in organizing and guiding the\ndevelopment of ideas. If the paragraphing were more reasonable, it could\neffectively improve the score.\nIn terms of vocabulary, the article generally performs well, with some\nadvanced words and phrases [comes down to one point | forces us to | look\nafter the needs of], but there are also some spelling and word choice errors\n[along the time / over time | tipycal | sourrounded | Nowadays | easyer |\ncottoges].\nThe range of grammatical structures is also somewhat limited. Although the\narticle uses complex sentence structures, including conditional clauses [if] and\n",
